    The upstream common components, compiled unmodified from the git submodule under
    ../upstream/egovframe-common-components into a jar: src/main/java and src/main/resources only.
    src/main/webapp (JSPs, static files, the bundled proprietary jars) is never packaged.

    The version is upstream's tag, not this project's: this artifact is upstream's code.
    Dependencies are upstream's pom, transcribed; versions come from the same parent upstream
    uses, imported as a BOM. Differences from upstream, all deliberate:
      - the bundled proprietary jar (smeapi) is optional: it cannot be published, and only cop.sms
        needs it;
      - the JDBC drivers are optional: which database a consumer talks to is the consumer's choice;
      - upstream's test dependencies are absent: its tests are not compiled here;
      - META-INF/LICENSE and META-INF/NOTICE are inside the jar;
      - the jar lacks the directory entry egovframework/com/cmm/service/ (see the exec step below).
